description: Code2Part project rules
alwaysApply: true
---

This is Code2Part, a React Native Expo TypeScript app for industrial product code identification and equivalent product comparison.

Target users:
- Technical salespeople
- Suppliers
- Purchasing staff with limited technical knowledge

Product goal:
The app should help users enter an industrial product code, understand what the product is, and compare possible equivalent product series.

This app is not:
- A CAD viewer
- A technical drawing tool
- A PDF parser
- A full ERP system
- A procurement marketplace

Current MVP scope:
- Local JSON mock data only
- No backend
- No Firebase
- No Supabase
- No authentication
- No payments
- No file upload

Initial supported products:
- Festo DSBC
- SMC CP96
- Product category: pneumatic cylinder
- Standard family: ISO 15552

Core flow:
1. Normalize product code.
2. Identify brand, series, category, standard family, and measurable attributes.
3. Extract bore and stroke from code when possible.
4. Find equivalent series using equivalence groups.
5. Show compatibility in simple Turkish.

Every technical attribute must include an evidence level:
- code
- series_table
- standard
- inferred
- unknown

Compatibility results must be separated into:
- compatible
- different
- unknownOrCheck
- warnings

Important:
Never show uncertain technical data as certain.
If a field cannot be verified, mark it as unknown or check required.
Avoid generic warnings when possible. Prefer field-level explanations.

Architecture rules:
- UI components must not contain domain logic.
- Resolver logic must live under src/domain/resolver.
- Mock catalog data must live under src/data.
- Shared types must live under src/types.
- Keep code modular, readable, and testable.
